.TH BACKUP-SEAFILE 1 "October 2026" "scripts" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
backup-seafile \- resilient encrypted incremental backup from Seafile to Google Drive via Rclone
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B backup-seafile
[\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR]
[\fB\-c\fR|\fB\-\-config\fR \fIFILE\fR]
[\fB\-\-setup-timer\fR]
[\fB\-\-remove-timer\fR]
[\fB\-\-status\fR]
[\fB\-\-force\fR]
[\fB\-\-dry-run\fR]
[\fB\-\-auto\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBbackup-seafile\fR synchronizes files from a \fBSeafile\fR instance (either via WebDAV \fBseafile-dav:\fR or a local FUSE mount like \fB/mnt/seafile-fuse\fR) directly to a Zero-Knowledge encrypted Google Drive destination (\fBgdrive-crypt:SeafileBackup\fR) using \fBrclone\fR.
.PP
Files and filenames are encrypted on-the-fly in RAM before reaching Google Drive. Only new and modified files are transferred (delta sync).
.PP
The utility is specifically architected for Linux server environments:
.IP \(bu 2
Can run completely headless without local FUSE mounts by streaming directly over Seafile WebDAV (\fBseafdav\fR).
.IP \(bu 2
Centralizes Google Drive authentication on a single backup server (supporting Google Service Account JSON keys).
.IP \(bu 2
Extracts "normal" filesystem hierarchies instead of proprietary Seafile/MinIO raw blocks and MySQL database dumps, ensuring fast zero-dependency disaster recovery.
.IP \(bu 2
Features systemd timer integration (both root system-wide and unprivileged user mode), flock concurrency guards, safe non-empty source verification, and optional syslog/webhook alerting.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Displays brief command-line help and exits.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " \fIFILE\fR"
Loads settings from a specified configuration file (overriding defaults in \fB/etc/seafile-backup.conf\fR or \fB~/.config/seafile-backup.conf\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-setup-timer
Installs and enables a resilient periodic systemd timer (\fBseafile-backup.timer\fR). If executed as root, installs system-wide to \fB/etc/systemd/system\fR; otherwise installs as a user service.
.TP
.B \-\-remove-timer
Stops, disables, and deletes the systemd service and timer.
.TP
.B \-\-status
Displays configuration, systemd timer status, cooldown state (last run and elapsed time), prerequisite health (network, Seafile endpoint, rclone), and recent log entries.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Forces an immediate backup run, bypassing cooldown interval and flock checks.
.TP
.B \-\-dry-run
Performs a trial run without transferring or writing any data to the remote.
.TP
.B \-\-auto
Automated execution flag used by the systemd service. Enforces cooldown restrictions and silent deferred exits when prerequisites are not met.
.SH ENVIRONMENT & CONFIGURATION
.TP
.B SEAFILE_SOURCE
Rclone WebDAV remote or local path (default: \fBseafile-dav:\fR).
.TP
.B RCLONE_DEST
Target encrypted remote and path (default: \fBgdrive-crypt:SeafileBackup\fR).
.TP
.B RCLONE_CONFIG_PATH
Optional path to an explicit \fBrclone.conf\fR file.
.TP
.B LOG_DIR
Directory for execution logs (default: \fB/var/log/seafile-backup\fR for root, \fB$HOME/.cache/rclone\fR for user).
.TP
.B BACKUP_INTERVAL_HOURS
Minimum cooldown interval in hours between automatic backups (default: \fB20\fR).
.TP
.B CHECK_INTERVAL
Systemd timer poll frequency (default: \fB15m\fR).
.TP
.B WAIT_ONLINE_TIMEOUT
Seconds to wait for network connectivity and Seafile endpoint at boot before deferring (default: \fB25\fR).
.TP
.B ALERT_WEBHOOK_URL
Optional HTTP webhook URL for JSON alert payloads upon backup completion or failure.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
Requires \fBrclone\fR, a configured \fBgdrive-crypt\fR remote, and access to Seafile via WebDAV or local mount.
